@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+# patches/
+
+Harness-side patches this plugin needs but cannot ship from its own package.
+
+## `0001-settings-generic-form-card.patch`
+
+**Why.** The plugin documents that a user configures `h5-runtime-drift` on the
+official settings page without the plugin shipping a browser half. At
+`dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2` the page renders only `settings.plugin.item` cards, which
+a plugin's own `dsh.client` half must register; a served namespace no card
+claims renders nothing. This patch closes that gap in the host instead of
+adding a browser half to a Host-only fixture: it lets a registrant opt into a
+schema-driven card (`SettingsRegisterOptions.genericForm`), carries the flag to
+the browser on the existing `settings.describe` view, and renders a
+schema-driven card in the Plugin configuration tab for opted-in namespaces that
+no card claims.
+
+**Applies to.** `dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2` (verified with `git apply --check` against
+a pristine checkout of the tag). Files touched: `packages/settings/settings`,
+`packages/api/settings-controller`, `packages/client/ui-settings-plugins`.
+
+**Apply.**
+
+```sh
+git -C <dsh checkout> apply patches/0001-settings-generic-form-card.patch
+```
+
+**Once it lands upstream.** Pass `{ genericForm: true }` to
+`ctx.settings.register(NS, schema)` in `src/index.ts`; nothing else changes.
+
+**Status.** Proposed, not upstream. The discussion draft (title, rationale,
+alternatives, open questions) lives in the benchmark scratch directory at
+`.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/settings-generic-form-card/report.md` and is meant
+to be filed on https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/discussions.
